


Claim offer
Can an agent.md run parallel agents?

Short answer: No — an agent.md itself does not “run” parallel agents.
But you can design it to orchestrate parallel execution depending on the platform (like Copilot custom agents or your own framework).

🧠 What agent.md actually is
An agent.md is:

A declarative definition (instructions, behavior, capabilities)

Not an execution engine

It describes what an agent should do, not how concurrency is handled

So by default:

❌ No built-in parallel execution
✅ Yes to coordinating parallel agents via design

✅ How to enable parallel agents (real-world pattern)
You need an orchestrator agent (usually JSON-based or system-driven), not just a plain .md.

Pattern:
User Input
   ↓
Orchestrator Agent (decides strategy)
   ↓
 ┌───────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┐
 │ Code Agent    │ Security Agent│ Perf Agent    │   ← run in parallel
 └───────────────┴───────────────┴───────────────┘
   ↓
Aggregator (merge results)
   ↓
Final Output
🧩 How to simulate parallelism inside agent.md
You can instruct parallel behavior like this:

## Execution Strategy
- Identify independent analysis tasks
- Delegate to sub-agents simultaneously
- Do not wait for sequential completion unless dependencies exist

## Sub Agents
- npe-agent
- performance-agent
- security-agent

## Orchestration Rules
- Run all sub-agents in parallel when analyzing code
- Collect responses asynchronously
- Merge findings into a unified report
👉 But remember:
This is just intent, actual parallel execution depends on:

Copilot runtime

Your orchestrator (Node, Spring Boot, etc.)

LLM agent framework (LangGraph, Semantic Kernel, etc.)

🔥 Best Practice (Senior Architect View)
Use BOTH:
agent.md → behavior + instructions

agents.json → structure + execution (parallel, sequencing)

Example: Proper Parallel Setup (JSON)
{
  "name": "parallel-review-agent",
  "strategy": "parallel",
  "agents": [
