👉 Use .md for behavior & intelligence

👉 Use .json for execution & orchestration (including parallelism)

🧠 The Real Difference (Think like an architect)
📄 .md → “Brain”
Defines:

Instructions

Reasoning style

Rules

Domain expertise

Example:

You are a senior Java reviewer.
Focus on null safety, clean code, and defensive programming.
👉 Great for:

LLM understanding

Readability

Iteration by humans

⚙️ .json → “Control Plane”
Defines:

Agent structure

Execution flow

Parallel vs sequential

Dependencies

Example:

{
  "name": "review-system",
  "strategy": "parallel",
  "agents": ["npe-agent", "security-agent"]
}
👉 Great for:

Orchestration

Automation

Tooling (Copilot, pipelines)

⚖️ When to Use Which
✅ Use .md ONLY when:
Single agent

No orchestration

You just need smart responses

👉 Example:

Code reviewer

Documentation assistant

✅ Use .json ONLY when:
You are wiring agents together

You need execution control

You want parallel processing

👉 Example:

PR review pipeline

Multi-agent system

